  body: "# Incompatible benefits in DMG chapter 17\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe chapter calls benefits incompatible
    where entitlement to one prevents entitlement to another, so there is no overlapping entitlement to adjust.\n\
    \n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThis definition does not identify every incompatible pair. Appendix 1 and the governing
    instruments must be checked. It must not be used as a synonym for a payment reduction or an overlap.\n\n## Inspected
    source passages\n\n- [DMG 17005, PDF page 2](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/62d7b8d5d3bf7f2865c6fe43/dmgch17.pdf#page=2)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 17: Overlapping benefits.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation of
    the 15 September 2026 source snapshot; unreviewed and requiring specialist review. The source is DWP guidance,
    not a consolidated statement of legislation. This is an independent experimental publication, not an official
    DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule.\n\nPDF page numbers are one-based file
    positions. Machine extraction can alter reading order, footnotes and characters. Quoted relationships preserve
    extracted text; no visual or specialist acceptance is claimed. Source dates, legal effects and current applicability
    remain separate review tasks.\n\n- `dmg-vol3-ch17` PDF SHA-256: `ce6967960168b301ae0b454df6824017202f6d3f6a14282a7ef0d4778bdac19a`;
    extracted pages SHA-256: `c00f0acadb11047d22fe6c046a756a164cc7be254aaebfb91470f2f38201af99`.\n"
